140	1506,351,1736,1346	Fig. 140.	A raceme of Lily of the Valley: a curving flower-stalk with nodding bell-shaped flowers on short pedicels, open below and in bud towards the top.
141	288,1652,418,2091	141. Spike.	Plan of a spike: an upright stem with flowers sitting directly on it, each in the axil of a small leaf-like bract.
142-143	463,1632,1095,2092	142. Raceme. 143. Corymb.	Left (142), plan of a raceme: nodding flowers on pedicels of equal length along a main stalk, above leafy bracts; right (143), plan of a corymb: long lower pedicels and short upper ones raise the flowers to a flat top.
144	1117,1635,1576,2091	144. Umbel.	Plan of an umbel: flower-stalks of equal length all springing from the top of the stalk, above a ring of bracts, and spreading to a rounded top.
